{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-brakewear fixture",
    "description": "The `process-brakewear` fixture: 750 rows of MOVESOutput -- brake-wear PM10 and PM2.5 AND running-exhaust Total Energy Consumption for passenger cars on urban restricted-access roads in Washtenaw County, August, 7am, 2020 -- computed from the snapshot's own INPUT tables. It ports docs/process-brakewear.md end to end and reuses the whole of docs/mixed-onroad.md's spine: the activity chain S1-S9, the cohort structure and the fuel-usage rebase S10-S12, the drive-cycle operating-mode weights `dc_W` and the base rate S13-S14, the calculator's adjustments S15 and the output row S16-S18. Brake wear is a rate on the same `BaseRateCalculator` spine, not a different model.\n\nWHAT IS NEW HERE, AND WHY THE DOCUMENT HAS A RELATION MIXED-ONROAD DOES NOT. mixed-onroad emits one pollutant-process, so `run_polProcessID` is a run-level scalar and every rate column is keyed by the cohort alone. This fixture emits three, and one cohort key -- the source bin's `shortModYrGroupID` -- DIFFERS between them: `pollutantprocessmodelyear` maps model year 2020 to short group 40 for 9101 and to 6 for 11609. A join key column has to be one-dimensional, so the rate stage is carried on a flat relation whose rows ARE the pollutant-process crossed with the cohort candidate grid -- `rate_rows`, 3 x 164, every factor a discovered extent, all its key columns one-dimensional (docs/esm-conventions.md 2). That is the whole structural difference; the arithmetic on it is mixed-onroad's, parameterised.\n\nCOMPUTED, from the input tables and nothing else: every number. `dc_W`, the speed-bin-weighted drive-cycle operating-mode distribution, is computed from `driveschedulesecond`'s 63,602 second-by-second speeds exactly as in mixed-onroad, and it is the SAME 46 weights for brake wear as for energy -- see docs/process-brakewear.md 3.2, where the mode-501 branch that would make them differ is shown to be project-scale-only. NO REFERENCE TABLE IS AN INPUT. `baserate_1_2020`, `baserate_9_2020`, `sourcebindistribution`, `sho` and `MOVESOutput` are all generator or expected output, and none of them is a `data_sources` entry here -- nothing flows from them into a number. Values out of the first three DO appear as `expected` in the inline tests below, which is the opposite direction and the whole point of a fixture.\n\nTHE PM10 BLOCK IS A CHAIN, NOT A SECOND RATE. `runspecchainedto` says 10609 <- 11609 and `pm10emissionratio` carries the ratio; the document reads both and never writes `106 = ratio x 116`. Its own rate path evaluates to EXACTLY 0 -- `emissionrate` has no 10609 row, so J22's inner join leaves the rate at the additive identity -- and its whole quantity arrives through a self-join of the rate relation on (chained-from pollutant-process, cohort). On an unchained row the chain key is 0 and the ratio is 0, so the same expression serves all three blocks with no branch.\n\nTWO CLAMPS, AND THIS TIME ONE OF THEM DOES NOT FIRE. At 59.5 degF the A/C activity term is -0.29698 and clamps to 0, as at mixed-onroad's 66.9 degF. The EV temperature term is +0.015625 and does NOT -- so the 84 energy/electricity rows carry a factor of 1.015625, and the arm docs/mixed-onroad.md 2.3(e) could only check in components/onroad_energy_output.esm is checked in a fixture here. Reaching it needed a lookup precedence mixed-onroad did not have: the one `temperatureadjustment` row is keyed regClassID 0, a WILDCARD, and adjust.rs:495-520 looks up the exact regulatory class first and that row second. mixed-onroad implements only the first step, gets zero terms, and reaches the same 1 by the clamp instead -- correct there, 1.56 % low here. The precedence is now lib/adjustments.esm's `exact_else_wildcard` and both fixtures instantiate it.\n\nDECLARED: one number, `n_outputCohort` = 125, the length of each output block's cohort run. WHICH 125 of the 164 candidates survive is a result of the chain and is never written down: `coh_rank` numbers them by an inclusive prefix count and the output row joins to that rank (docs/esm-conventions.md 22). Three counts keep it honest and one of them is new: `cohortSurvivorCount` recomputes 125, `pp_selectedCohortCount` recomputes it SEPARATELY for each pollutant-process -- 125, 0, 125, the zero being the chained one -- and `run_chainedRowCount` counts the 125 rows that arrive through the chain. The comparator's exact key set fails on any row whose rank found no cohort.\n\nTHE PACKED IDENTIFIER IS NEVER BUILT, ONLY UNPACKED. `emissionrate`'s 60,388 rows carry `sourceBinID` = 1e18 + fuel x 1e16 + engTech x 1e14 + regClass x 1e12 + shortModYrGroup x 1e10, past 2^53. `lib/onroad_activity.esm`'s `source_bin_slot` reads the four components out; nothing here composes one, and no element type is declared for the same reason (finding F18).",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "moves",
      "onroad",
      "brakewear",
      "pm",
      "fixture",
      "process-brakewear"
    ]
  },
