      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "the_run_scope_comes_from_the_execution_database",
          "description": "Year 2020, August, hour 7, source type 21, road type 4, county 26161, zone 261610. The RunSpec XML says month 7 and hour 6; the execution database says 8 and 7, and it is the authority (docs/mixed-onroad.md 0.1). 59.5 degF is the hour's temperature and its heat index -- the two columns are equal in every row of this snapshot and the document still reads them separately, because adjust.rs uses the first for the temperature adjustment and the second for the A/C term and the EV suppression.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "run_yearID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 2020.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_monthID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 8.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_hourID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 7.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_sourceTypeID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 21.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_roadTypeID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 4.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_countyID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 26161.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_zoneID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 261610.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_stateID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 26.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_baseYearIsAnalysisYear",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_fuelYearID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 2020.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_hpmsVtypeID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 25.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_daysInMonth",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 31.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_monthGroupID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 8.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_temperature",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 59.5,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_heatIndex",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 59.5,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the_three_pollutant_processes_and_the_chain_between_them",
          "description": "The run's whole pollutant scope, unpacked from `runspecpollutantprocess` and `runspecchainedto` rather than written down. 9101 is Total Energy x Running Exhaust and is the only ENERGY pollutant here, so it is the only one S18 divides by 1,055,055.9; 11609 is PM2.5 Brakewear x Brakewear and carries its own emissionrate rows; 10609 is PM10 Brakewear, which carries NONE and is chained from 11609. `rspp_chainInputPolProcessID` is 11609 on the middle row and 0 on the other two, and that 0 -- the additive identity of the LEFT JOIN, which is no pollutant-process -- is what makes the chain term vanish without a branch.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "rspp_pollutantID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 91.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_pollutantID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 106.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 2
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_pollutantID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 116.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 3
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_processID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_processID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 9.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 2
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_processID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 9.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 3
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_isEnergy",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_isEnergy",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 2
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_isEnergy",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 3
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_unitDivisor",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1055055.9,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_unitDivisor",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 2
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_unitDivisor",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 3
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_chainInputPolProcessID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_chainInputPolProcessID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 11609.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 2
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_chainInputPolProcessID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 3
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the_drive_cycle_scaffolding_is_a_single_physics_row_and_two_data_thresholds",
          "description": "The three facts W's correctness rests on that are not W itself: the braking thresholds are READ from operatingmode's Braking row rather than written as drivecycle.rs's -2.0 and -1.0 literals; exactly one physics-mapping row is selected, so dss_vsp is one polynomial and not a sum of several; and every average-speed bin's bracketing weights sum to 1, which is what catches a duplicated bracket speed or a bin with no bracket.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "run_brakeRate1Sec",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": -2.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_brakeRate3Sec",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": -1.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_physicsRowsSelected",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_fuelUsageWildcardCount",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 5.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "asb_scheduleFractionTotal",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "avgspeedbin_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "asb_scheduleFractionTotal",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "avgspeedbin_rows": 8
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "asb_scheduleFractionTotal",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "avgspeedbin_rows": 16
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the_cohort_row_set_is_the_same_125_for_both_rate_paths",
          "description": "125 of the 164 candidates survive `stmyFraction > 0`, and all 125 reach an emissionrate row, for BOTH computed pollutant-processes -- which is the claim that lets one cohort rank serve all three output blocks and is asserted rather than assumed. `pp_selectedCohortCount` is 125, 0, 125: the middle zero is the chained pollutant, which has no pollutantprocessmodelyear rows and therefore no source-bin distribution of its own, and whose 125 output rows come from the chain instead -- `run_chainedRowCount` counts them. `run_cohortSelectionTotal` at 250 is the same fact summed, and would still be 250 if the two rate paths selected DIFFERENT 125s, which is why the per-pollutant-process counts are asserted beside it.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "cohortSurvivorCount",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 125.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_cohortSelectionTotal",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 250.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_chainedRowCount",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 125.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "pp_selectedCohortCount",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 125.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "pp_selectedCohortCount",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 2
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "pp_selectedCohortCount",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 125.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 3
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "pp_rateCohortCount",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 125.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "pp_rateCohortCount",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 2
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "pp_rateCohortCount",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 125.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 3
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the_drive_cycle_weights_are_a_distribution_over_the_twenty_three_running_modes",
          "description": "W, checked on the two properties that do not require the reference. It is a DISTRIBUTION: the weights sum to the avgSpeedFraction column's own total, which is 1 to that column's six stored significant figures and not exactly, so the gate is ABSOLUTE at 1e-5 and not relative (docs/esm-conventions.md 20.5). And it covers exactly 23 operating modes.\n\nTHE MODE COUNT IS THE BRAKEWEAR-SPECIFIC ASSERTION HERE. `emissionrate` carries a 11609 rate for operating mode 501, `brakewear;stopped`, and `opmodepolprocassoc` associates it with 11609 -- so a reader may reasonably expect brakewear's weight vector to be 24 modes wide. It is not: drivecycle.rs:235-237 assigns a zero-speed second to mode 501 only at PROJECT scale and to mode 1 otherwise, this run is Inventory scale, and 24 here would mean the classification had taken the wrong branch. docs/process-brakewear.md 3.2 has the measurement.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "tolerance": {
            "abs": 1e-05
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "dc_WTotal",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "dc_WTotal",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
